# Version Tagging (SemVer)

Format: `v1.2.3` (`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`)

Applies to **all** repositories in the monitoring project (`monitoring`, `monitoring-worker-go`, `monitoring-website`, `monitoring-agent`, etc.).

| Change type | Bump |
| --- | --- |
| Bugfix or very small tweak only | **PATCH** (3rd digit): `v1.2.3` → `v1.2.4` |
| New functionality / feature | **MINOR** (2nd digit): `v1.2.3` → `v1.3.0` |
| Very large changes or breaking / incompatible with previous version | **MAJOR** (1st digit): `v1.2.3` → `v2.0.0` |

## When tagging or bumping versions

- Choose the bump from the **nature of the change**, not from commit count.
- After a MINOR or MAJOR bump, reset lower digits to `0`.
- Do not invent a different scheme; keep the `v` prefix.
